# Design system

Tailwind v4, **CSS-first**. There is no `tailwind.config.js` and adding one is the wrong
move — everything lives in `src/styles/globals.css`.

## The design is deliberately not the shadcn default

The previous version of this site looked generic, and the cause was well-documented
defaults: neutral slate palette, 8px radius on everything, default type sizes, a muted
indigo accent, 1px card borders. Those are the recognisable fingerprint of an untuned
component library. Each has been deliberately moved:

| Default tell | What this site does |
|---|---|
| slate/zinc neutrals | faintly **cool** neutrals — and explicitly not warm cream, which now reads as generic AI output |
| `--radius: 0.5rem` | **`--radius: 0`**. Sharp corners everywhere |
| default Inter | a three-face system, see below |
| muted indigo accent | a **teal** accent, used sparingly |
| flat surfaces | grain overlay, hairline grid field, sunken panels |

Do not reintroduce these. If a component looks "off", tune the token, not the primitive.

## Typography — three faces, three jobs

| Face | Job | Token |
|---|---|---|
| **Newsreader** | display + long-form prose | `--font-serif` |
| **Geist Sans** | UI, nav, lists, cards | `--font-sans` |
| **Geist Mono** | labels, metadata, numbers, tags | `--font-mono` |

All **self-hosted** variable woff2 in `src/public/fonts/`, ~171 KB total.
**Never replace these with a Google Fonts link** — zero third-party requests is a hard
constraint (ADR-0004). A new face must be downloaded into the repo.

Scale contrast is doing real work: `--text-display` runs to 5.5rem while body stays at
1rem. That gap is what stops a single-column page reading as an unstyled document.

## Signature devices

These carry the design. Use them rather than inventing new ornament.

- **`.label`** — mono, uppercase, letterspaced, tabular. Section headings, metadata keys,
  tags, dates. The site's most recognisable element.
- **The rail** — a 10rem left column at ≥1024px holding section numbers and labels
  (`Section` in `Layout.tsx`). It varies horizontal placement, which is the main defence
  against single-column monotony.
- **`.grid-field`** — hairline CSS grid, radially masked. Behind heroes only.
- **`.newthought`** — small-caps opening words. Preferred over a drop cap, whose
  browser support is still poor.
- **`.prose-editorial`** — serif long-form setting for case studies.
- **Grain** — one fixed `body::before` overlay at ~3% opacity.

## Theming

Tri-state: light / dark / **system by default**, and system is CSS-only. No class on
`<html>` means follow the OS. `.light` / `.dark` override. The dark palette appears
twice — once in the media query, once under `.dark` — because plain CSS cannot share a
block between them. **Keep them in sync.**

## Colour is verified, not eyeballed

Values are load-bearing. Every foreground clears WCAG AA against its surface, and every
colour is inside the sRGB gamut — the light accent's chroma sits exactly at the sRGB
maximum for its lightness and hue, so raising it clips rather than saturates.

```bash
yarn check:contrast
```

Run it after changing any colour. It parses the CSS directly, so it cannot drift.

## shadcn

Still used for primitives (`src/components/ui/`). Generate them:

```bash
yarn dlx shadcn@latest add <component>
```

Then tune via tokens. `--radius-*` all map to `0`, so generated components inherit the
sharp treatment automatically.
